# This repo has no root-level env vars. Each app/package that needs
# environment config keeps its own .env.example, copy the ones you need:
#
#   apps/web/.env.local.example        -> apps/web/.env.local
#   apps/mobile/.env.example           -> apps/mobile/.env
#   packages/import-job/.env.example   -> packages/import-job/.env
#
# apps/web/.env.local.example
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL       Supabase project URL
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  Supabase anon (public) key
#
# apps/mobile/.env.example
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL       Supabase project URL
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  Supabase anon (public) key
#
# packages/import-job/.env.example
#   SUPABASE_URL                  Supabase project URL
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY     Supabase service role key (never expose to clients)
#
# Local Supabase stack (supabase/config.toml) is started with the Supabase CLI
# (`supabase start`) and does not require a .env file; it prints the local
# URL/keys to use above once running.
